_raw_eligibility_text:
Ages Eligible for Study: 18 Years and older.
Sexes Eligible for Study: All.
Accepts Healthy Volunteers: No.

Inclusion Criteria:
Male or female >= 18 years old;
Life expectancy >= 12 weeks;
Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status 0-1;
Patients with histologically or cytologically confirmed diagnosis of inoperable locally advanced or recurrent/metastatic NSCLC with EGFR mutations. Patients must have progressed from or be intolerant to or be unfit for standard treatment.
For dose escalation: patients with documented EGFR mutation that have progressed on or after third-generation EGFR-TKI. In addition, other lines of therapy may have been given.
For dose expansion and Phase II: patients with EGFR C797S mutation confirmed prior to enrollment on tissue or blood samples with radiological documentation of disease progression from first-generation, second-generation or third-generation EGFR-TKIs. In addition, other lines of therapy may have been given;
For dose expansion and Phase II, patients must have at least one measurable tumor lesion per RECIST v1.1 criteria as per Investigator's assessment;
Adequate bone marrow, liver, and renal function:
Blood: Absolute neutrophil count (ANC) >= 1.5 x 10^9/L, platelets count >= 100 x 10^9/L, hemoglobin >= 9 g/dL (must not have received transfusion or granulocyte colony-stimulating factor within 2 weeks of screening);
Liver function: total bilirubin <= 1.5 x ULN; ALT and AST <= 3.0 x ULN; if liver metastases exist, AST and ALT <= 5.0 x ULN; for documented Gilbert's syndrome, total bilirubin <= 3.0 x ULN;
Renal function: eGFR >= 50 mL/min (CKD-EPI);
All acute toxic effects of any prior antitumor therapy or surgery resolved to baseline or <= CTCAE Grade 1 (except alopecia);
For women of childbearing potential, negative serum pregnancy test within 7 days before dosing, non-lactating; contraception throughout treatment and 3 months after last dose;
Men with partners of childbearing potential willing to use adequate contraception during study and 90 days after last dose;
Patients must have signed informed consent form.

Exclusion Criteria:
Presence of another active primary malignant tumor;
Unstable, symptomatic primary CNS tumors/metastasis or leptomeningeal metastases not suitable for enrollment; a patient may enroll if clinically stable, no imaging progression within 2 weeks prior to first dose, and off corticosteroid/anticonvulsant/mannitol for longer than 2 weeks prior to first dose;
Treatment with most recent therapy (chemotherapy, immunotherapy, targeted therapy, radiation, investigational agent) within 4 weeks or approximately 5 half-lives, whichever is longer, before first dose;
Gastrointestinal disorders affecting oral swallowing or drug absorption;
Use of strong or moderate CYP3A inhibitors or inducers within 7 days prior to first dose;
Autologous (within 3 months) or allogeneic (within 6 months) organ or stem cell transplantation prior to first dose; any major surgery or severe trauma (except biopsy) within 4 months prior to first dose;
Palliative radiation therapy within 2 weeks prior to first dose;
Active viral hepatitis B (exception: HBV DNA <= 500 IU/mL stable longer than 4 weeks);
Active infection requiring systemic therapy within 1 week prior to first dose;
Cardiac conditions within the last 6 months: unexplained/cardiovascular presyncope or syncope, tachycardia, ventricular fibrillation, sudden cardiac arrest; prolonged QTcF > 450 msec (males) or > 470 msec (females);
Any > CTCAE Grade 1 toxicity prior to first dose;
Medical history of interstitial lung disease, drug-induced ILD, radiation pneumonitis requiring steroids, or clinically active ILD, any uncontrolled systemic disease, or other serious illnesses;
Deep venous thrombosis, pulmonary embolism, or other serious thromboembolism within 3 months prior to first dose (implantable port, catheter-related, or superficial venous thrombosis not considered serious);
Presence of drug abuse and medical, psychological, or social conditions that do not permit protocol compliance.
